The Q4_K mat-vec formulation becomes a property of the model a child serves rather than of
the process it runs in. `Q4K_VARIANT` 3 compiles from the pinned commit's own shader text --
the packed16 scale decode, the top-tested superblock loop, and the sixteen-fma minimum term
the activation group-sum member replaced -- so its module is bit-identical to the module a
build of the pinned commit creates, and `ggml_vk_load_shaders` selects it whenever
`GGML_VK_Q4K_VARIANT` is absent. A release carrying every formulation therefore serves the
production kernel to every row that names nothing, and a row-scoped arm moves that row alone.

The route is `--vk-q4k-variant KEY` with `LLAMA_ARG_VK_Q4K_VARIANT` as its `set_env`, so the
key reaches a child through its own preset section the way the six tuple keys do. A router
argv would push one value onto every section through `common_preset::merge`, and a process
environment variable would reach every child from the router's `environ` snapshot, so neither
carries a per-row claim; `tools/server/server.cpp` sets `GGML_VK_Q4K_VARIANT` from the parsed
value in its non-router branch alone, ahead of `common_params_print_info` and therefore ahead
of the first `ggml_vk_get_device` call that `ggml_vk_load_shaders` runs inside. `setenv`
overwrites, so the section's key wins over an ambient one.

`production` admits `/4` alone. `NUM_ROWS` reaches the shader as specialization constant 1
and the dispatch as the pipeline's workgroup denominator, `evidence/q4k-scale-decode/`
reproduces the four-row ISA of every arm and no receipt measures the pinned formulation at
two or eight rows, and the census decode ledger records `constants=64,4,1`. A name or a row
count outside the admitted set ends the load through the existing `GGML_ABORT` rather than
serving the default under an arm's name.

